# Options of rynas-web, read by rynas-web.service (EnvironmentFile).
# Apply changes with: systemctl restart rynas-web

# Address and port of the web interface. The default listens on every IPv4
# interface, since a NAS is usually headless and reached over the LAN.
# Use [::]:8080 for IPv4 and IPv6 (fails if IPv6 is disabled in the kernel),
# or 127.0.0.1:8080 behind a reverse proxy on the same host.
# The connection is plain HTTP for now: do not expose this port to the
# Internet (HTTPS comes in a later release).
RYNAS_WEB_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:8080

# Extra command line options, for example:
#   --secure-cookies            behind an HTTPS reverse proxy
#   --admin-group GROUP         who is an administrator (repeatable; replaces
#                               the defaults rynas-admin and sudo)
#   --session-idle-timeout SEC  default 1800
#   --session-max-age SEC       default 43200
# See /usr/libexec/rynas/rynas-web --help
RYNAS_WEB_OPTS=""
